<title>FRANCE: French industrial production rises in December.</title>
<headline>French industrial production rises in December.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE said on Friday industrial production, excluding construction, rose 0.6 percent in December from the previous month and was up 2.0 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Industrial production excluding energy, agri-food businesses and construction -- considered by INSEE the best measure of manufacturing output -- rose 0.8 percent in December from the previous month, giving a year-on-year rise of 1.1 percent.</p>
<p>It gave the following seasonally adjusted data based on an index introduced in January 1996 (percentage change)</p>
<p>						    Dec 96  Nov 96  y/y</p>
<p>Industrial production index (base 1990)*  0.6    0.0    2.0</p>
<p>Manufacturing output			    0.8   -0.5    1.1</p>
<p>  Agri-food					-0.4    2.4    2.1</p>
<p>  Energy					    0.2    0.6    6.9</p>
<p>  Semi-finished goods			   0.0   -0.2    2.6</p>
<p>  Industrial capital goods		    0.7   -0.6    1.0</p>
<p>  Car industry				   -0.3   -1.5   -1.0</p>
<p>  Consumer goods				  4.1   -0.7   -1.6</p>
<p>  Construction				    3.7   -2.6   -4.5</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following seasonally adjusted index figures:</p>
<p>					Dec 96   Nov 96  Oct 96   Dec 95</p>
<p>Industrial production index   100.2     99.6     99.6    98.3</p>
<p> Manufacturing output	    95.9     95.1     95.6    94.4</p>
<p> Agri-food			  111.5    112.0    109.4   109.4</p>
<p> Consumer goods		    98.1     94.2     94.9    96.8</p>
<p> Car industry		     101.3    101.6    103.1   104.0</p>
<p> Industrial capital goods	86.0     85.4     85.9    85.1</p>
<p> Semi-finished goods	     99.9     99.9    100.1    97.2</p>
<p> Energy			     119.1    118.9    118.2   114.1</p>
<p> Construction			89.4     86.2     88.5    91.9</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom + 33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
